# motoquencer `constantlength = 2`: skip is also the CURRENCY the compensation
# pays in, not just something it reacts to. motoquencer.md:922 — "also the *skip*
# setting of steps is honored and modified in order to keep the length constant.
# A skipped step essentially has the length 0 (or 0 repeats)."
#
# Every step starts at 1 repeat, so there is no room to shorten anything by
# lowering repeats (the floor is 1). Raising step 1 to 2 repeats therefore has to
# be paid for by SKIPPING the next step in the search — step 2 — which is exactly
# the "length 0" the manual describes. The cycle stays 4 clocks.
#
# SPEC-GAP (documented in seqcore.hpp): the manual never says which way round to
# spend. A step's capacity to give is its full repeat count at level 2 (reach 0 by
# skipping it) and one less at level 1 (the floor is 1), and the skip is only used
# when the whole step is owed — a partial debt is taken out of repeats instead.
#
# Dialling step 1 back down to 1 repeat then owes a clock the other way, and the
# first candidate the forward search meets is the skipped step 2: un-skipping it
# hands back exactly its 1 repeat. Un-skip is the mirror of skip.
tickrate 100
patch <<<
[m4]
[motoquencer]
    clock          = I1
    fadermode      = I2
    constantlength = I3
    reset          = I4
    numsteps       = 4
    numfaders      = 4
    quantize       = 0
    cvbase         = 0
    cvrange        = 1
    defaultgate    = 1
    cv             = O1
>>>
@2 move F1 0.0
@3 move F2 0.25
@4 move F3 0.5
@5 move F4 0.75
@6 set I2 3
@7 set I3 2
# step 1: 1 -> 2 repeats (notch 1). Nothing has repeats to spare, so step 2 is
# skipped to pay for it.
@8 move F1 0.0666667
@8 expect F1 0.0666667 tol 1e-4
@8 expect F2 0 tol 1e-4
@9 set I2 0
# 4 clocks per cycle: step 1 twice, (step 2 skipped), steps 3 and 4 once.
@11 set I1 1
@11 expect O1 0 tol 1e-4
@12 set I1 0
@13 set I1 1
@13 expect O1 0 tol 1e-4
@14 set I1 0
@15 set I1 1
@15 expect O1 0.5 tol 1e-4
@16 set I1 0
@17 set I1 1
@17 expect O1 0.75 tol 1e-4
@18 set I1 0
@19 set I1 1
@19 expect O1 0 tol 1e-4
@20 set I1 0
# now step 1: 2 -> 1 repeats. The clock owed goes to the skipped step 2, which is
# un-skipped to absorb it.
@22 set I2 3
@23 move F1 0.0
@23 expect F1 0 tol 1e-4
@23 expect F2 0 tol 1e-4
@24 set I2 0
# reset, so the second reading starts cleanly on step 1 again
@25 set I4 1
@26 set I4 0
# 4 clocks again, and step 2 is back in the sequence.
@28 set I1 1
@28 expect O1 0 tol 1e-4
@29 set I1 0
@30 set I1 1
@30 expect O1 0.25 tol 1e-4
@31 set I1 0
@32 set I1 1
@32 expect O1 0.5 tol 1e-4
@33 set I1 0
@34 set I1 1
@34 expect O1 0.75 tol 1e-4
@35 set I1 0
